{{#if (or (ne elixirDeploy "none") (ne elixirClustering "none"))}}
## Releases

Use Elixir 1.17 or newer.
{{#if (ne elixirDeploy "none")}}
The Docker builder pins Elixir 1.20.4 and OTP 29.0.6.
{{/if}}

```sh
MIX_ENV=prod mix deps.get --only prod
MIX_ENV=prod mix release
_build/prod/rel/{{elixirAppName}}/bin/{{elixirAppName}} start
```

Release settings are read at startup through `config/runtime.exs` and `rel/env.sh.eex`.
Keep `mix.lock` with the project and review dependency updates before rebuilding a release.
{{#if (ne elixirDeploy "none")}}
The generated Dockerfile can be built with `docker build -t {{elixirAppName}} .`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (ne elixirWebFramework "none")}}
Set `SECRET_KEY_BASE` and `PHX_HOST` in the deployment environment before starting the release.
{{/if}}
{{#if (ne elixirClustering "none")}}

### Clustering

Set `RELEASE_COOKIE` to the same private value on every node. Set a unique, reachable
`RELEASE_NODE` such as `{{elixirAppName}}_a@10.0.0.10` on each node. The release enables long node
names; it refuses to start without a cookie. Keep Erlang distribution on a private network.

{{#if (eq elixirClustering "libcluster")}}
For Docker, Gigalixir, and standalone Mix releases, set `CLUSTER_HOSTS` to comma-separated full
node names. The EPMD strategy reconnects every second. Alternatively, set `DNS_CLUSTER_QUERY`
to a DNS name whose addresses correspond to `{{elixirAppName}}@<address>` nodes. Explicit hosts
take precedence over DNS. Empty discovery settings leave the node unclustered.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq elixirClustering "dns-cluster")}}
DNSCluster polls `DNS_CLUSTER_QUERY` every five seconds and connects to `{{elixirAppName}}@<address>`
for each A or AAAA record it returns. Node basenames must match. An empty query leaves the node
unclustered.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq elixirClustering "distributed-erlang")}}
`{{elixirModuleName}}.Cluster` calls `Node.connect/1` for every node in `CLUSTER_HOSTS`
(comma-separated full node names) at startup and every five seconds. There is no automatic
discovery; list each peer explicitly. An empty list leaves the node unclustered.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq elixirDeploy "fly")}}

Fly uses the application's internal DNS and `FLY_PRIVATE_IP` automatically. Set the same
`RELEASE_COOKIE` secret on its machines. Its release uses IPv6 Erlang distribution.
{{/if}}

Gigalixir must supply a unique `RELEASE_NODE` and the shared cookie in its release environment.
Choose discovery values that resolve inside that application's private network. These settings
do not provision machines or certify a hosted deployment.
{{/if}}

{{/if}}
{{#if (eq elixirJobs "exq")}}
## Exq jobs

Exq stores jobs in Redis. Start Redis and set `REDIS_URL` (default `redis://localhost:6379`)
before `mix phx.server` or `iex -S mix`. Enqueue the sample job with
`{{elixirModuleName}}.Workers.SampleWorker.enqueue("Ada")`. Tests use `Exq.Mock` and need no Redis.
{{/if}}

{{#if (ne elixirLogging "none")}}
## Logging

{{#if (eq elixirLogging "logger-json")}}
LoggerJSON formats every `Logger` call as one JSON object per line, including `request_id`
metadata. Run `mix run -e 'require Logger; Logger.info("hello")'` to see the output.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq elixirLogging "logger-file-backend")}}
LoggerFileBackend appends `info` and higher log lines to `log/{{elixirAppName}}.log`, alongside the
console output. Change the path or level under `config :logger, :file_log`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq elixirLogging "logster")}}
Logster replaces Phoenix's request log with one logfmt line per request, for example
`method=GET path=/api/health status=200 duration=0.412`.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

{{#if (ne elixirConfig "none")}}
## Runtime configuration

`{{elixirModuleName}}.Settings` reads `APP_GREETING` (default `Hello`) and `APP_MAX_CONNECTIONS`
(integer, default `10`) from the environment.
{{#if (eq elixirConfig "dotenvy")}}
Dotenvy loads `.env` and the process environment in `config/runtime.exs`; real environment
variables win. Read values with `{{elixirModuleName}}.Settings.greeting()` and
`{{elixirModuleName}}.Settings.max_connections()`.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq elixirConfig "skogsra")}}
Skogsra reads and casts each variable on first use and caches it. Read values with
`{{elixirModuleName}}.Settings.greeting!()` and `{{elixirModuleName}}.Settings.max_connections!()`;
call `reload_max_connections/0` after changing the environment.
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq elixirConfig "confex")}}
`config/config.exs` declares `{:system, ...}` tuples that Confex resolves on every read. Read values
with `{{elixirModuleName}}.Settings.config()`.
{{/if}}

```sh
APP_MAX_CONNECTIONS=25 mix run -e 'IO.inspect({{elixirModuleName}}.Settings.{{#if (eq elixirConfig "skogsra")}}max_connections!(){{else if (eq elixirConfig "confex")}}config(){{else}}max_connections(){{/if}})'
```
{{/if}}

{{#if (ne elixirMessageQueue "none")}}
## Message broker

{{#if (eq elixirMessageQueue "amqp")}}
`{{elixirModuleName}}.MessageQueue` publishes to and reads from the durable RabbitMQ queue
`{{elixirAppName}}.greetings` at `RABBITMQ_URL` (default `amqp://guest:guest@localhost:5672`).

```sh
docker run -d --name rabbitmq -p 5672:5672 rabbitmq:4-alpine
```
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq elixirMessageQueue "gnat")}}
`{{elixirModuleName}}.MessageQueue` publishes to and subscribes on the NATS subject
`{{elixirAppName}}.greetings` at `NATS_URL` (default `nats://localhost:4222`).

```sh
docker run -d --name nats -p 4222:4222 nats:2-alpine
```
{{/if}}
{{#if (eq elixirMessageQueue "brod")}}
`{{elixirModuleName}}.MessageQueue` creates the Kafka topic `{{elixirAppName}}.greetings` when it is
missing, produces to partition 0, and fetches the record back. Set `KAFKA_BROKERS` to a
comma-separated `host:port` list (default `localhost:9092`). brod compiles a small NIF, so a C
compiler is required.

```sh
docker run -d --name kafka -p 9092:9092 apache/kafka:latest
```
{{/if}}

With the broker running:

```sh
mix run -e 'IO.inspect({{elixirModuleName}}.MessageQueue.round_trip("hello"))'
mix test --include message_queue
```

Plain `mix test` skips the broker test.
{{/if}}

